{"node_id": "symbol:netbox/utilities/ordering.py:naturalize:19", "symbol": "naturalize", "type": "function", "file": "netbox/utilities/ordering.py", "lines": [19, 48], "source": "def naturalize(value, max_length, integer_places=8):\n    \"\"\"\n    Take an alphanumeric string and prepend all integers to `integer_places` places to ensure the strings\n    are ordered naturally. For example:\n\n        site9router21\n        site10router4\n        site10router19\n\n    becomes:\n\n        site00000009router00000021\n        site00000010router00000004\n        site00000010router00000019\n\n    :param value: The value to be naturalized\n    :param max_length: The maximum length of the returned string. Characters beyond this length will be stripped.\n    :param integer_places: The number of places to which each integer will be expanded. (Default: 8)\n    \"\"\"\n    if not value:\n        return value\n    output = []\n    for segment in re.split(r'(\\d+)', value):\n        if segment.isdigit():\n            output.append(segment.rjust(integer_places, '0'))\n        elif segment:\n            output.append(segment)\n    ret = ''.join(output)\n\n    return ret[:max_length]", "calls": [], "called_by": ["naturalize_interface"], "confidence": 0.92, "purpose": "Take an alphanumeric string and prepend all integers to `integer_places` places to ensure the strings", "behavior_patterns": ["ACCUMULATE(re.split('(\\\\d+)', va... -> output segment rjust)"], "semantic_contract": {"purpose": "Take an alphanumeric string and prepend all integers to `integer_places` places to ensure the strings", "language": "python", "symbol_name": "naturalize", "symbol_type": "function", "signature": "(value, max_length, integer_places)", "bases": [], "class_attrs": {}, "raises": [], "uses": [], "behavior_patterns": ["ACCUMULATE(re.split('(\\\\d+)', va... -> output segment rjust)"], "tier": 1, "calls": [], "called_by": [{"source": "symbol:netbox/utilities/ordering.py:naturalize_interface:51"}], "comple